{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity","id":1404625,"title":"Maintaining Humanity?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-25T13:21:04-07:00","id":1404625,"title":"Maintaining Humanity?","content":"How do you help keep your character from losing their humanity in your story?<br /> *(This topic assumes a character wants to maintain their humanity in the first place.)<br /> <br /> Playing my character in our DAV20 game, had me realize that over hundred and thousands of years, pretty much all vampires will start sliding down a slippery slope and losing more and more of their humanity. The years and the things whey have to do to survive, just chips away at even the most moral of kindred kind.<br /> <br /> While I know some vampires would use roads in place of humanity or devote themselves to certain pursuits. How do most/some vampires keep their humanity?<br /> <br /> For example, in my character's case, due to his backstory or the lack of one (<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">amnesiac). He come to treat all his ghouls like family and actually fell in love with one. In a way, his ghouls are his anchor to humanity and losing them would likely make him fall hard down the humanity scale.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> But I am wondering, what other ways or means can a vampire do to help them maintain their humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","user":"Wingstorm","date":".  Spelling corrections 07-25-2020, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T13:32:53-07:00","id":1404627,"title":"","content":"In my DAV20 all vampire are using a variant of the Path of the Kings because it is beside using the Path of Christ the only one where you can justify self denfense. Every other path collides with the Bloodlines statement, that killing in Self Defense is not costing humanity because they say as vampire no matter what intention if it is not path of a road it cost you. So if you do not want to play the hard way or do an only pacifistic researcher chronic like an option in The Age of Decadence the only other way would be houserule that Self Defense is not costing humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-25-2020, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T13:43:32-07:00","id":1404631,"title":"","content":"The only way to maintain high humanity is to avoid vampire society as a whole, and not engage in any activity that may make you do morally dubious things like killing people. In other words, avoid most of the activities that players want to do when they play in an RPG.<br /> <br /> I do think it is possible for an ST to run an interesting game with one PC that is fun while allowing that PC to maintain high humanity. However, I think it is much harder in an actual group because too many other players will want to do things that conflict with high humanity. So that PC would constantly be opting out of the coterie's activities. Much harder for an ST to run, and likely not fun for the player or even the entire group of players. But every gaming group is different, and some could do it.<br /> <br /> Maintaining high humanity is HARD, and takes constant effort. It becomes a goal in and of itself. And in order to do so, the character likely has to adopt some form of spiritual exercise or discipline so that it helps him overcome the natural moral failures that will occur over time, and rededicate himself to his spiritual goals as opposed to giving up.<br /> <br /> Note, if I was ST running your game, the fact you even have ghouls would be an obstacle for you to maintain high Humanity. Because you enslaved them by making them ghouls. No matter how well you treat them, or that the blood screws with their mind so much that they're &quot;fine&quot; with what you've done. So it's still a greatly morally compromising act. That might be fine for a Humanity 6 or 7, but would be a real problem for something higher than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T20:38:02-07:00","id":1404699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404631#post1404631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note, if I was ST running your game, the fact you even have ghouls would be an obstacle for you to maintain high Humanity. Because you enslaved them by making them ghouls. No matter how well you treat them, or that the blood screws with their mind so much that they're &quot;fine&quot; with what you've done. So it's still a greatly morally compromising act. That might be fine for a Humanity 6 or 7, but would be a real problem for something higher than that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel I should give some more context to my character's current situation. Any advice on how I can roleplay him better is much appreciated. <br /> <br /> Well, my character is at humanity 6. My ST made it clear that even humanity 7 is difficult to maintain for a vampire with ghouls. <br /> <br /> For some context on my character's situation. While he started out quite naive about ghouling, having lost all his memories. He sees ghouling as a gift and a means to forge a bond. He does eventually realise it is just slavery in another name. After having a number of his ghouls died due to a wave of the black death, where he was really emotionally crushed, he pretty much could never bring himself to have another ghoul since. The black death and his ghouls dying was particularly painful for him. He almost lost his lover in that plague and I remembered telling my ST that if he wasn't able to save his lover, he would likely just walk into the Sun. Unwilling to go on without the person he loved the most. <br /> <br /> As for his ghoul lover, who is his oldest surviving ghoul, the thing is, for the longest time (in story, about 1~2 centuries) my character was extremely guilt ridden over never being able to give his lover the choice of actually being his lover. He just doesn't know if the love they shared is real, or solely due to the blood bond and given his ghoul's age, he can't just free him from the blood bond to find out. <br /> <br /> That is... Until certain recent events made him realise that his lover ghoul is actually... bond resistant. Their blood bond degrades naturally to that of a 2 sips after every week or two. His lover could actually have broken free pretty much at any time. All this time, he thought his lover's almost weekly request for blood was just them being close and didn't thought more of it.<br /> <br /> Being a Tremere... He actually went and did some research when he found out that his lover is bond resistant. &quot;Testing&quot; the limits of their bond, to confirm that his lover actually stayed with him out of a genuine want and not solely due to their bb. This whole discovery is both a relief (that their relation is not due only to a bb) and terrifying, cos if they are not careful, some other kindred can blood bond his lover. (Since his lover's BB3 only last about a week or two)<br /> <br /> I actually discussed with my ST on my character and we both come to the conclusion that my character would have been a much more powerful and &quot;better&quot; Tremere vampire if he wasn't so tied down by his lover and him caring so much for his ghouls.<br /> But playing VTM had made me realise that unlike D&amp;D it's not so much about winning, but enjoying the story that comes from roleplaying, interactions and acting out your character's motivations.<br /> <br /> So while I think my character's struggle to maintain his humanity, may be a disadvantage in kindred society and that his story has some tragic elements or the potential for tragically in it, I feel that it is what makes my character interesting and I would really like to continue roleplaying my character well.<br /> <br /> Would be grateful for any advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26067,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","user":"Wingstorm","date":". 07-25-2020, 11:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T08:52:41-07:00","id":1404783,"title":"","content":"The point of the game is that the PCs become inhumane monsters, but feel fine with that situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T09:52:27-07:00","id":1404791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404699#post1404699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel I should give some more context to my character's current situation. Any advice on how I can roleplay him better is much appreciated.<br /> <br /> Well, my character is at humanity 6. My ST made it clear that even humanity 7 is difficult to maintain for a vampire with ghouls.<br /> <br /> For some context on my character's situation. While he started out quite naive about ghouling, having lost all his memories. He sees ghouling as a gift and a means to forge a bond. He does eventually realise it is just slavery in another name. After having a number of his ghouls died due to a wave of the black death, where he was really emotionally crushed, he pretty much could never bring himself to have another ghoul since. The black death and his ghouls dying was particularly painful for him. He almost lost his lover in that plague and I remembered telling my ST that if he wasn't able to save his lover, he would likely just walk into the Sun. Unwilling to go on without the person he loved the most.<br /> <br /> As for his ghoul lover, who is his oldest surviving ghoul, the thing is, for the longest time (in story, about 1~2 centuries) my character was extremely guilt ridden over never being able to give his lover the choice of actually being his lover. He just doesn't know if the love they shared is real, or solely due to the blood bond and given his ghoul's age, he can't just free him from the blood bond to find out.<br /> <br /> That is... Until certain recent events made him realise that his lover ghoul is actually... bond resistant. Their blood bond degrades naturally to that of a 2 sips after every week or two. His lover could actually have broken free pretty much at any time. All this time, he thought his lover's almost weekly request for blood was just them being close and didn't thought more of it.<br /> <br /> Being a Tremere... He actually went and did some research when he found out that his lover is bond resistant. &quot;Testing&quot; the limits of their bond, to confirm that his lover actually stayed with him out of a genuine want and not solely due to their bb. This whole discovery is both a relief (that their relation is not due only to a bb) and terrifying, cos if they are not careful, some other kindred can blood bond his lover. (Since his lover's BB3 only last about a week or two)<br /> <br /> I actually discussed with my ST on my character and we both come to the conclusion that my character would have been a much more powerful and &quot;better&quot; Tremere vampire if he wasn't so tied down by his lover and him caring so much for his ghouls.<br /> But playing VTM had made me realise that unlike D&amp;D it's not so much about winning, but enjoying the story that comes from roleplaying, interactions and acting out your character's motivations.<br /> <br /> So while I think my character's struggle to maintain his humanity, may be a disadvantage in kindred society and that his story has some tragic elements or the potential for tragically in it, I feel that it is what makes my character interesting and I would really like to continue roleplaying my character well.<br /> <br /> Would be grateful for any advice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interessting. Is this some houserule or pre V20 supplement merrit because I only know from Ghouls and Revenants, that there is a merrit for being totally unable to be bond but about a fast unbounding I read nothing.<br /> Though I do not know how common the knowledge is in the world but in the V20 core rule book it states that love through blood bound is the closest to true love that is available so if she would have no problem to stay with him the blood bound would only strenghten her feelings while at the same time would prevent her from being stolen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T19:15:28-07:00","id":1404864,"title":"","content":"Humanity isn't all that hard to maintain as a vampire, but it is very difficult to maintain in a vampire game.<br /> <br /> By this I am referring to the fact that game storylines are by default designed to be engaging and filled with drama. Said drama usually comes with choices that test ones humanity, which is how vampire tend to lose their humanity. This is especially the case if the ST is using above average vampire population numbers in their games.<br /> <br /> A vampire can easily go decades, if not a century between major ethical crisis as long as the character build and game are not focused on being a monster of the week style of setup. On the other hand a tremere who resides in a chantry built on top of an archeological dig site, basically can spend years doing his research and only running into the local town for the occasional snack. The closest you get to an ethical crisis is if the Tremere wants to play hero and interrupt a bar brawl or take a talented local mortal under their wing as a possible recruit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T06:51:06-07:00","id":1404914,"title":"","content":"Though it is to say, that embracing is ruled on murder it the intented person died by either his hand, some other hand or a natural cause like disease, accident or age because if you give him still blood while his body is warm it works.<br /> So yeah for Tremere there is an alternative option of a ritual which inject blood into a ghoul if he dies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T07:40:52-07:00","id":1404919,"title":"","content":"Double Post because of connection probleslms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T09:14:34-07:00","id":1404929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404791#post1404791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interessting. Is this some houserule or pre V20 supplement merrit because I only know from Ghouls and Revenants, that there is a merrit for being totally unable to be bond but about a fast unbounding I read nothing.<br /> Though I do not know how common the knowledge is in the world but in the V20 core rule book it states that love through blood bound is the closest to true love that is available so if she would have no problem to stay with him the blood bound would only strenghten her feelings while at the same time would prevent her from being stolen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe my character's ghoul resistance to being blood bond is a houserule or my ST's self made story element. We are using a modified version of V20/DAV20. <br /> That said, I believe V5 has something similar, where you can make your character resistance to being bloodbond?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T09:18:46-07:00","id":1404930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404864#post1404864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity isn't all that hard to maintain as a vampire, but it is very difficult to maintain in a vampire game.<br /> <br /> By this I am referring to the fact that game storylines are by default designed to be engaging and filled with drama. Said drama usually comes with choices that test ones humanity, which is how vampire tend to lose their humanity. This is especially the case if the ST is using above average vampire population numbers in their games.<br /> <br /> A vampire can easily go decades, if not a century between major ethical crisis as long as the character build and game are not focused on being a monster of the week style of setup. On the other hand a tremere who resides in a chantry built on top of an archeological dig site, basically can spend years doing his research and only running into the local town for the occasional snack. The closest you get to an ethical crisis is if the Tremere wants to play hero and interrupt a bar brawl or take a talented local mortal under their wing as a possible recruit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. We do have quite a number of combat situations in the game (spread in game over centuries). The funny thing is that my character kinda got shaped by in-game events into a sort of battle mage. And is able to use thaumaturgy to strengthen himself for combat.<br /> <br /> The threat of a moral/ethical crisis is quite real and haven popped up a number of times in the story so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T09:49:56-07:00","id":1404933,"title":"","content":"You hover at humanity 4 or 5. If for some rare reason you drop to 3 (probably due to diablerie) it's time to get religious (until you find yourself at 4 or 5 again) The best way to keep your humanity is to have a high conscience rating....<br /> <br /> I'm just kidding of course. The sanest way to retain humanity is to obfuscate 3 yourself as a celebrity and make unannounced visits to the section of the hospital that houses terminally ill children. You can be the person that these kids want to meet, and they will cherish that memory for the rest of their short lives, and then you try not to cry (because that in itself is emotionally powerful stuff, not because you took the 'thirst for the innocent' flaw)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-27-2020, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T11:08:46-07:00","id":1404945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404929#post1404929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe my character's ghoul resistance to being blood bond is a houserule or my ST's self made story element. We are using a modified version of V20/DAV20.<br /> That said, I believe V5 has something similar, where you can make your character resistance to being bloodbond?</div> </div> </div> </div>I looked up. Yeah they have beside a hardcore V20 Tremere version (where one sip bound you already) and the immun against it another version where you automatically loose one point of the bound every full or new moon (so within one month you get from full bound to just one sip)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T13:12:08-07:00","id":1404967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404929#post1404929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I believe my character's ghoul resistance to being blood bond is a houserule or my ST's self made story element. We are using a modified version of V20/DAV20. <br /> That said, I believe V5 has something similar, where you can make your character resistance to being bloodbond?</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has a 5 dot merit that makes you immune to the blood bond. It\u2019s for vampires but a ST could easily give it to a ghoul. Btw in V5 the blood bond only activates if you drink directly from the regnant. So you can easily have ghouls Who are not blood bound to anyone or vampires who drink vitae without fear of enslavement or to become a diablerist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T16:27:22-07:00","id":1404986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1404930#post1404930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lol. We do have quite a number of combat situations in the game (spread in game over centuries). The funny thing is that my character kinda got shaped by in-game events into a sort of battle mage. And is able to use thaumaturgy to strengthen himself for combat.<br /> <br /> The threat of a moral/ethical crisis is quite real and haven popped up a number of times in the story so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I figured it was something like that.<br /> <br /> I tend to play my characters like Xanatos with fangs. So in the case of a Tremere character, he wouldn't so much enter into direct combat as lead the enemy into a situation where they more or less defeat themselves. A particular favorite is creating a false chantry which is just a total death trap, but there is a hidden passage say across the street to the real chantry. Worst case scenario the enemy burns down the false chantry and believes they have won, or you use a self destruct.<br /> <br /> Then again I firmly believe that no elder worth their salt would even enter into a situation where they haven't won before showing up. But that once again tends to run contrary to the style of vampire game where the Lost Boy Brujah are throwing down with bunch of preppy Ventrue in an abandoned construction site or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T09:24:42-07:00","id":1405076,"title":"","content":"To me VtM treated 'humanity' as the label for the 'Vampire path for goodness/morality' rather than reflecting human nature. Or at most, it reflects a particular (narrow) subset of humanity (which isn't surprising when you consider how 'non-western' alternatives got treated in, say, Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom.) Humans can be pretty diverse (and even subjective) in how they define good/evil (across time, culture, or any number of factors) and I have always felt 'humanity' should reflect this as well (representing a series of 'paths' different from Sabbat oriented paths) - it may not inherently be 'good' but it brings you closer to human rather than vampiric nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T23:22:38-07:00","id":1405131,"title":"","content":"The way I see it, vampires struggle with two urges: the urge to glut themselves when even slightly hungry, and the urge to smash anything that makes them even slightly angry. &quot;Humanity&quot; is whatever set of beliefs help them to resist those two urges.<br /> <br /> &quot;I will not glut myself when even slightly hungry or smash anything that makes me even slightly angry because that would be evil&quot; works, because it's constantly reinforced by the human culture that surrounds them.<br /> <br /> Things like, &quot;I will not glut myself when even slightly hungry or smash everything that makes me slightly angry because that is not conducive to the cunning and aware predator I aspire to be&quot; also works, but is harder because it is not reinforced by the surrounding human culture. You pretty much have to immerse yourself into a cult of like minded vampires to make such things work and be reinforced externally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T16:01:01-07:00","id":1405209,"title":"","content":"I kind of visualize it as when someone is embraced, the human emotional programming, gets another species emotional setup imposed on it. The human emotions tend to be emphatic, social, and self-aware. The vampire emotion set is more like that of a hunting spider. Not self aware, not social and totally without any empathy or pity for other creatures. Over time, the human emotions erode, and the vampire set grows stronger.<br /> <br /> Most neonates tend to have the human set dominant almost all the time. Brief episodes of frenzy are the exception. But over time, if you let your human side abrade, lose the pity and emotional and social connection with other people, the human side will wither and the vampire becomes more and more dominant. The ultimate expression of this process has no human side and no self-awareness at all -a wight.<br /> <br /> So actively working on your social and emotional connections to people around you can slow or stop the decline. An elder who is far gone can still manage to continue his existence if he can find some ember of human emotion inside himself and fan it into some kind of human feeling.<br /> <br /> Vampires tend to disassociate and consider the alien emotional set as something &quot;other&quot; -the beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T21:45:44-07:00","id":1405245,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I had someone who started their PC at Humanity 9. The problem was the player\u2019s extremely self-focused (Humanity 9 was ultimately because \u201cI\u2019m a special snowflake, pay attention to me\u201d) so they ended up pulling a couple of actions that despite their conscience 4 resulted in a pair of botches (I\u2019m using the DAV20 rules where the difficulty is the difference between the path and the sin... and these were basically callous disregard for human life with humanity 9 as the start point) and a failure.<br /> <br /> So in the course of three sessions the\u2019ve dropped to Humanity 6, Conscience 2... but the PLAYER doesn\u2019t know it because I do all that rolling... and frankly they\u2019d probably have a fit that getting the Scourge sicced on an innocent dhampir runaway to curry favor with the Prince because they wanted to hold a charity benefit concert (with themselves as the star performance) would be a \u201cyou fail humanity forever\u201d level breach... because it was to get a charity benefit concert for needy children and they didn\u2019t \u201cknow\u201d the Prince would send in the Scourge when they gave the location of the Dhampir to the Prince... they just REALLY wanted permission for that benefit concert (to promote themselves).<br /> <br /> Anyway the plan is to just to start describing how they\u2019re looking paler and they\u2019re feeling hungrier than usual (because now blush of life isn\u2019t free) and see how long it takes them to figure out what\u2019s going on. The player also believes they should be able to buy True Faith soon (because THEY are so faithful and the Faith is so important to THEM... I hope I am properly conveying the narcissism of their statements).<br /> <br /> TL;DR... if you want to maintain a high humanity in game... it helps to actually have one outside the game too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T00:18:14-07:00","id":1405254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405245#post1405245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope I am properly conveying the narcissism of their statements).</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel for you, brother. As a player and ST in many Vampire chronicles, I share your pain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:24:11-07:00","id":1405260,"title":"","content":"But aren't high humanity vampires meant to be insufferable people? <br /> <br /> The one high humanity character I had was from normally pretty good player who knows his stuff, but he played a <i>Gio-Fucking-Vani. </i>At first I laughed and just thought he wanted a challenge or a game of personal horror. The pressures of the family and necromancy weighing down her soul.... Many games in, when she's got a complete Vicissitude job and hiding from the family in a Bahari cult, I discover he originally intended for a fun lighthearted game where his high-humanity self insert would travel the world collecting artifacts and not do anything bad despite her occupation and bloodline... <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:24:32-07:00","id":1405261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405245#post1405245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I had someone who started their PC at Humanity 9. The problem was the player\u2019s extremely self-focused (Humanity 9 was ultimately because \u201cI\u2019m a special snowflake, pay attention to me\u201d) so they ended up pulling a couple of actions that despite their conscience 4 resulted in a pair of botches (I\u2019m using the DAV20 rules where the difficulty is the difference between the path and the sin... and these were basically callous disregard for human life with humanity 9 as the start point) and a failure.<br /> <br /> So in the course of three sessions the\u2019ve dropped to Humanity 6, Conscience 2... but the PLAYER doesn\u2019t know it because I do all that rolling... and frankly they\u2019d probably have a fit that getting the Scourge sicced on an innocent dhampir runaway to curry favor with the Prince because they wanted to hold a charity benefit concert (with themselves as the star performance) would be a \u201cyou fail humanity forever\u201d level breach... because it was to get a charity benefit concert for needy children and they didn\u2019t \u201cknow\u201d the Prince would send in the Scourge when they gave the location of the Dhampir to the Prince... they just REALLY wanted permission for that benefit concert (to promote themselves).<br /> <br /> Anyway the plan is to just to start describing how they\u2019re looking paler and they\u2019re feeling hungrier than usual (because now blush of life isn\u2019t free) and see how long it takes them to figure out what\u2019s going on. The player also believes they should be able to buy True Faith soon (because THEY are so faithful and the Faith is so important to THEM... I hope I am properly conveying the narcissism of their statements).<br /> <br /> TL;DR... if you want to maintain a high humanity in game... it helps to actually have one outside the game too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with what you did but for one thing: you should have told the player about the drop in humanity imo. Not telling him/her about such an important development is bound to cause problems down the line despite the ruling being absolutely correct.<br /> <br /> Losing 3 points of humanity and going from 9 to 6 is a big deal as it dramatically changes the PCs expected behaviour and its very &quot;essence&quot; and the player should be informed about it even if his/her action entirely warranted the drop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:40:31-07:00","id":1405265,"title":"","content":"At the very least, I feel you should have told the player about the unreal amount of satisfaction they (the beast) felt doing the bad thing and hope the player understands the hint.<br /> <br /> I do think a high conscience is pretty in line with narcissism. The 'I can never do anything wrong' should stave off the beast quite well.<br /> <br /> I made Narcissism a 'merit' in my game: conscience at the cost of self control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T01:45:39-07:00","id":1405267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405261#post1405261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree with what you did but for one thing: you should have told the player about the drop in humanity imo. Not telling him/her about such an important development is bound to cause problems down the line despite the ruling being absolutely correct.<br /> <br /> Losing 3 points of humanity and going from 9 to 6 is a big deal as it dramatically changes the PCs expected behaviour and its very &quot;essence&quot; and the player should be informed about it even if his/her action entirely warranted the drop.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think it's a good idea to hide a character's Humanity score from their player.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can understand the intent is to be &quot;realistic&quot;, because most folk are unaware of their moral degeneration.<br /> <br /> But I still think the need to be open and transparent with a player is more important than enforcing character ignorance with player ignorance. It's a Social Contract thing.<br /> <br /> Because if the player would theoretically pitch a fit about being made to roll degeneration, how much more of a fit do you think they'll pitch LATER when it finally comes out that they were losing Humanity fast and the ST was keeping that information from them?<br /> <br /> I <i>guarantee</i> it won't end well. This is the kind of thing that causes fights, in Real Life.<br /> <br /> Communication at the table is important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:32:00-07:00","id":1405345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405267#post1405267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">^This.<br /> <br /> I honestly don't think it's a good idea to hide a character's Humanity score from their player.<br /> <br /> Yes, I can understand the intent is to be &quot;realistic&quot;, because most folk are unaware of their moral degeneration.<br /> <br /> But I still think the need to be open and transparent with a player is more important than enforcing character ignorance with player ignorance. It's a Social Contract thing.<br /> <br /> Because if the player would theoretically pitch a fit about being made to roll degeneration, how much more of a fit do you think they'll pitch LATER when it finally comes out that they were losing Humanity fast and the ST was keeping that information from them?<br /> <br /> I <i>guarantee</i> it won't end well. This is the kind of thing that causes fights, in Real Life.<br /> <br /> Communication at the table is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Sins of the Blood (okay it is written from a point of a True Brujah) it is said, the higher your humanity the more you feel alive. This is in line with the higher the humanity the earlier you wake up and the later you go to sleep. It is part of feelable how hard blush of life is to maintain. So yeah it should be told to the player how high his humanity is to reflect how the vampire feels.<br /> I mean like I said before Path of Humanity is how guilt ridden you feel so it should be actually shown immedeataly, if you for example feel no guilt anymore in stealing should show clearly how high it is. Problem you feel normally how guilty you feel but because your humanity is different from your characters it should always be showable about what you feel guilty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T09:01:08-07:00","id":1405354,"title":"","content":"I for one remain annoyed that the -how much earlier you rise- aspect of humanity has never been written down. Is it ten minutes a dot or does it depend on the climate or...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:18:51-07:00","id":1405382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405354#post1405354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I for one remain annoyed that the -how much earlier you rise- aspect of humanity has never been written down. Is it ten minutes a dot or does it depend on the climate or...</div> </div> </div> </div>Well VTMV is at least partly doing this. On Humanity 9 you can rise one hour after sunrise and one before sunset, on 8 only one hour before sunset, and so I say RAI on Humanity 7 you rise and fall with the fall and rise of the sun and each further humanity down is putting another hour down one sunrise/set. It only retcons which I find fair, that for humanity 10 vampires staying awake during the day would be like staying awake for humans at the night.<br /> <br /> Edit: Though then for example Humanity 1 Vampires would be only able to stay awake for one hour during summer solstice so it is mayby not such a great idea so whatever each person fits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":26160,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","user":"Koronus","date":". 07-30-2020, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:41:22-07:00","id":1405387,"title":"","content":"low humanity vampires functionally wouldn't be able to do anything if you use hours like that. nights are short","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:47:02-07:00","id":1405389,"title":"","content":"Yeah on the shortest night during summer solstice is only 7 hours and the longest night during winter solstice is 16 hours (in austria). Mayby with the earlier rising it whas only for high huminaty vampires. But we can only work what we got and as you said, before VTMV it whas never written down before what has been actually ment on how earlier high humanity vampires can rise.<br /> Though it would fit with how low humanity vampires would mainly spent time in Torpor because they find it hard to stay awake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T18:36:02-07:00","id":1405441,"title":"","content":"On the topic of hiding a character's humanity rating from a player. Isn't that counter productive? Shouldn't a player know their character's humanity rating, so they know how to roleplay their character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T02:55:09-07:00","id":1406082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mister_Dunpeal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1405076#post1405076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To me VtM treated 'humanity' as the label for the 'Vampire path for goodness/morality' rather than reflecting human nature. Or at most, it reflects a particular (narrow) subset of humanity (which isn't surprising when you consider how 'non-western' alternatives got treated in, say, Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom.) Humans can be pretty diverse (and even subjective) in how they define good/evil (across time, culture, or any number of factors) and I have always felt 'humanity' should reflect this as well (representing a series of 'paths' different from Sabbat oriented paths) - it may not inherently be 'good' but it brings you closer to human rather than vampiric nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire has always been a pretty explicitly Judeo-Christian myth based game, so Humanity is pretty directly based on that same conceptual frame. You can certainly change that, but it pulls up a lot of the mythic underpinnings of the game when you do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26347-bladedancer","name":"Bladedancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T03:41:10-07:00","id":1406084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladedancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406082#post1406082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampire has always been a pretty explicitly Judeo-Christian myth based game, so Humanity is pretty directly based on that same conceptual frame. You can certainly change that, but it pulls up a lot of the mythic underpinnings of the game when you do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This again...<br /> <br /> No aspect of the mythology of Vampire is Christian; Nadda, zilch. It's strictly old-testament. The series pays as much attention to Muslims as it does to Christians, so the &quot;judeo-christian&quot; phrase, coined to basically mean &quot;Abrahamic but without islam&quot; is just the wrong term for the game. The game is more Gnostic than anything (but few people know what that means, so it's not surprising it hasn't caught on). Christianity would give us a nice, benevolent God. Judaism and Gnosticism give us what we've got in the WoD.<br /> <br /> The first two editions of vampire said &quot;morality is chosen, not ordained&quot; and, while that has died and later had it's corpse mutilated, being a good moral person and getting God's forgiveness was never the mentality players were expected to have. It was an option, but not a smart one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:26:35-07:00","id":1406095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406084#post1406084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This again...<br /> <br /> No aspect of the mythology of Vampire is Christian; Nadda, zilch. It's strictly old-testament. The series pays as much attention to Muslims as it does to Christians, so the &quot;judeo-christian&quot; phrase, coined to basically mean &quot;Abrahamic but without islam&quot; is just the wrong term for the game. The game is more Gnostic than anything (but few people know what that means, so it's not surprising it hasn't caught on). Christianity would give us a nice, benevolent God. Judaism and Gnosticism give us what we've got in the WoD.<br /> <br /> The first two editions of vampire said &quot;morality is chosen, not ordained&quot; and, while that has died and later had it's corpse mutilated, being a good moral person and getting God's forgiveness was never the mentality players were expected to have. It was an option, but not a smart one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue its not really Gnostic.<br /> <br /> It's just God is an asshole. There's no Demiurge because there's not a higher God above God, it's just the entire universe is ruled by a jerk.<br /> <br /> I'd argue it's closest to Warhammer 40K.<br /> <br /> There's the evil demons and then they're opposed by the Emperor....who is either missing, dead, or was a jerk to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T06:53:57-07:00","id":1406104,"title":"","content":"That's... you not entirely understanding Gnostic thought. With Gnostic thought, the thing is that higher Gods don't really come into/concern themselves with reality (which includes all the umbras and probably includes the far out stuff) Reality seems pretty well shielded from outsiders. Gnosticism has this idea of Emanations; Divine things from outside of reality that fall into reality, decline, and then rise up and out of reality. Perhaps Caine is an Emanation, and perhaps the Demiurge got to curse caine for entering his playground: You could infer True faith and certain other things as being sourced from outside of reality; A good bit of Gnosticism entered Christianity with the idea that the God from the old testament is the evil demiurge and the nice God Jesus represents is the True, real god from up high (one needs only imagine the Anti-semetism this line of thought would cause; But you could also imagine how it applies to the Sabbat's worship of Caine. Gnosticism was eventually deemed heretical and purged by the church) <br /> <br /> The Thematically Gnostic part of the old VTM editions was that, well, you could try to become human, but a big part of the Vampire species is the desire to fight the opperession from above and eat your way up; to unshackle yourself from earthly limitations. The Beast might've been an anchor but the morality of God was optional; you could grow to chose your own morality. It's all very nietzche. The Punk aspect of VTM was deeply Gnostic, and the Gothic aspect was... it fitted the bill too. Of course this sentiment was lessened come revised for a more conventional morality and is gone now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T16:55:18-07:00","id":1406180,"title":"","content":".... So I'm going to retract my point in the face of MyWifeis Scary, because that is a *much* more detailed theological analysis than I was offering. I would argue there's a fair bit more Catholic apocrypha in it than you're crediting, but Gnostic (or Deistic if you want to get more Reformation about it) philosophy is definitely a richer frame for VtM than strictly conventional Christian myth. <br /> <br /> Also, damn.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26347-bladedancer","name":"Bladedancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T03:12:55-07:00","id":1406245,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bladedancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406180#post1406180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">....there's a fair bit more Catholic apocrypha in it than you're crediting,</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I'm interested, but at the same time; apocrypha is apocrypha. To quote wikipedia; <span style=\"color:#202122\"> In general use, the word </span><i>apocrypha</i><span style=\"color:#202122\"> came to mean &quot;false, spurious, bad, or heretical.&quot; and, to a degree, different denominations of christianity designated old, secret, often jewish texts as apocrypha. With that out of the way; Tell me more. </span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:27:22-07:00","id":1406269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406084#post1406084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The series pays as much attention to Muslims as it does to Christians, so the &quot;judeo-christian&quot; phrase, coined to basically mean &quot;Abrahamic but without islam&quot; is just the wrong term for the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might come as a surprise to many real-world Muslims who are RPG fans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:36:10-07:00","id":1406271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406269#post1406269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This might come as a surprise to many real-world Muslims who are RPG fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry I failed the english test skill and the hobby knowledge WoD roll. Can you please elaborate why it is a surprise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T08:04:07-07:00","id":1406274,"title":"","content":"I don't think they feel included. At least not included as much as Christians, or that the Muslim faith gets as much attention as in the game as does Christianity. And the fact much of the attention it gets is to make a fetish of the faith or outright negative.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T10:28:59-07:00","id":1406291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1404625-maintaining-humanity?p=1406274#post1406274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least not included as much as Christians, or that the Muslim faith gets as much attention as in the game as does Christianity. And the fact much of the attention it gets is to make a<b> fetish of the faith</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I get that. The negative perspective is really a 1e, but revised, v20 and v5 have put Islam on a perverse pedestal. <br /> <br /> The thing is though, that's kinda how they've done Christians, who're either bigoted zealots or perfect nuns you 